title: jq fzf powered filtering excerpt
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

When needing to explore a JSON file for a long time I just reached into my `history` and looked for a oneliner that I copied from a [[github gist|https://github.com/fiatjaf/awesome-jq#command-line]] `echo '' | fzf --print-query --preview "cat *.json | jq {q}"`. This worked quite well, but I have now decided to improve it leveraging the fzf features.

